# Show help
if [ "$FIRST_ARG" = "-h" ] || [ "$FIRST_ARG" = "--help" ]; then
    cat <<EOF
repostatus - Git repository manager with multi-system dotfiles sync

USAGE:
  $(basename "$0")              Interactive TUI mode (default)
  $(basename "$0") --sync       Sync all dirty repositories
  $(basename "$0") --commit     Commit all dirty repositories
  $(basename "$0") --dotfiles   Sync dotfiles (host-specific branches)
  $(basename "$0") --json-summary  JSON output for Waybar

DOTFILES SYNC:
  Manages dotfiles across multiple systems using per-host git branches.

  Architecture:
    master           - primary machine (ArchyTux) source of truth
    host-<hostname>  - secondary machines: sync from master, customizations only

  Branch strategy:

  Workflow (smart auto-discovery):
    1. Detects hostname → manages host-<hostname> branch
    2. Fetches master, updates local master
    3. Scans for local changes vs master
    4. Already customized files: kept as-is
    5. New local changes: asks user to keep or sync to master
    6. Kept files: auto-added to custom list for future syncs
    7. Host→branch mapping maintained automatically

  Philosophy: Unified dotfiles by default. Only host-specific when necessary.

  Config files (auto-created):
    - ~/.config/repostatus/dotfiles-custom-files (discovered custom files)
    - ~/.config/repostatus/dotfiles-hosts (host to branch reference)

